# ---- Xcode project ----
# TextMate.xcodeproj is COMMITTED (Phase 2 Task 7): project.yml stays the
# source of truth, but contributors need only Xcode, not XcodeGen, to build.
# Regenerate on demand with `xcodegen generate --spec project.yml` after
# editing project.yml. xcuserdata/*.xcuserstate below still ignore the
# per-user state XcodeGen writes on every `xcodegen generate` and every
# `open TextMate.xcodeproj`.
#
# Xcode/generated/TextMate.entitlements (XcodeGen's `entitlements:` plist
# output, from project.yml's static `properties:` block) is COMMITTED too,
# for the same reason as the .xcodeproj itself: the TextMate target's
# CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS build setting points at this exact path, so a
# fresh clone that never runs `xcodegen generate` -- which every doc now
# says is optional -- would otherwise fail ProcessProductPackaging with a
# missing file (found by testing an actual clean build, Phase 2 Task 8).
# Its content is fully deterministic from project.yml; regenerate and
# re-commit it alongside the .xcodeproj if `entitlements:` ever changes.

# ---- Legacy upstream artifact ----
Frameworks/license/src/revoked_serials.cc

# ---- Xcode user state ----
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout
.swiftpm/

